In Geddam Jhansi v. State of Telangana17, the Hon'ble Supreme Court held as follows;
"In the context of matrimonial disputes, emotions run high, and as such in the complaints filed alleging harassment or domestic violence, there may be a tendency Peeta Newton vs The State Of Andhra Pradesh on 26 September, 2025 Indian Kanoon - http://indiankanoon.org/doc/97115308/
5 to implicate other members of the family who do not come to the rescue of the complainant or remain mute spectators to any alleged incident of harassment, which in our view cannot by itself constitute a criminal act without there being specific acts attributed to them.
